# EAS Build uploads this Git folder; when this file exists it is used instead of the .gitignore files.
#
# Why it is needed: eas-cli on Windows does not apply .gitignore files in subfolders (it compares
# "folder/" with "folder\..." paths), so it tried to upload smart-tourist-server/.demo-db (locked
# by the running demo database) and smart-tourist-mobile-app/android (a stale local build that
# would make EAS skip its own prebuild). Rules here are relative to this folder.

# Only the mobile app is needed to build the APK.
# (No trailing "/" on folder rules: eas-cli checks folder paths without one, so "x/" never matches.)
/*
!/smart-tourist-mobile-app

# Same exclusions as smart-tourist-mobile-app/.gitignore
node_modules
.expo
dist
web-build
expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
app-example
/smart-tourist-mobile-app/ios
/smart-tourist-mobile-app/android
